                <pb facs="0658" n="560" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg560"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Choate</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic">January 16,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Ascertain and cable the status of American cargoes on the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Maria</hi>, the <hi rendition="#italic">Mashona</hi>, and the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Beatrice</hi>, so Department may inform shippers where
                    their goods are and what portion of them are free.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
